# Future Design Note — Assistant Read-Only API

## Goal

Add a small read-only API layer that allows an AI assistant to inspect the plant tracking system safely.

This is not part of the current stage. It is a future convenience feature for debugging, review, planning, and guidance.

The assistant should be able to answer questions like:

- what photos exist for this growing unit?
- what happened around this date?
- show the recent evidence for this plant/batch/location
- which photos are unclassified?
- what notes/events are linked to this photo?

## Scope

Include read-only assistant endpoints for:

- photos
- growing units
- locations
- notes
- events
- summary/export views
- optional thumbnails

Do not include write access at first.

## Non-goals

This does not include:

- direct database access
- raw SQL access
- delete/update endpoints
- irrigation/control actions
- automatic public sharing
- unrestricted full-resolution photo dumps

## Proposed endpoints

```text
GET /assistant/summary
GET /assistant/photos
GET /assistant/photos/{photo_id}
GET /assistant/photos/{photo_id}/context
GET /assistant/photos/{photo_id}/thumbnail
GET /assistant/growing-units
GET /assistant/growing-units/{id}/context
GET /assistant/locations
GET /assistant/events
GET /assistant/unclassified
